Resource capability
-------------------

The resource capability owns resource lifecycle, format selection, canonical
GPU-free shader/reflection models, and the format readers under
`src/resource/formats`. Copied format implementations retain their original
license and notice files under `format-notices/<format>/`, including notices
for meshoptimizer, yaml and black-reader-js; the ww2ogg-translated Wwise Vorbis
repacker and codebook data (BSD 3-clause); and the stb_vorbis-derived Huffman
setup. See THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md. The WEM reader's PTADPCM decoder was
removed on 2026-10-11 until its provenance can be confirmed; PTADPCM media is
identified but not decoded.

The bundled Black definition JSON files are generated CarbonEngineJS schema
artifacts produced by `tools-core` from Carbon's Blue exposure declarations.
Their generator revisions, digests and retention purpose are recorded in
`docs/resource/formats/provenance.md`; they contain no Carbon source and no game
asset.

The GR2/GSF reader was migrated after its EUPL-derived decoder was replaced by
a validated clean-room implementation and the donor was relicensed MIT. The
modern cFSD decoder and reviewed dataset schemas decode caller-supplied bytes
and include no acquired game data, decoded tables, or native loader modules.
The legacy 32-bit FSD loader under `src/resource/formats/fsd/32` ports
CarbonEngine's open-source `fsd` library (MIT); it reads caller-supplied bytes
against a caller-supplied schema and ships no schemas. See
`format-notices/fsd`.

Shader and effect pipeline
--------------------------

The runtime reads compiled EVE effect files and translates their shaders for
WebGPU and WebGL2. Each part rests on published material:

- Effect container: CarbonEngine's compiled-effect format, published by
  Fenris Creations (CCP Games) as open source under the MIT License. The codec
  in `src/resource/format/carbonEffect` ports `Tr2EffectRes.cpp` and the
  shader compiler's file assembly. The layout was already known from ccpwgl.
  See `format-notices/hlsl`.
- Shader compiler: `src/shadercompiler` ports CarbonEngine's
  `trinity/shadercompiler` (MIT); see THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md.
- Compiled shader bytecode: Microsoft's DXBC format, which Microsoft publishes
  in DirectX-Headers (MIT) and the DirectX Shader Compiler. See
  `format-notices/dxbc`.
- Translation: the WGSL and GLSL emitters re-express what a shader computes so
  a browser can run the same effect. Game shaders' HLSL source is not used. The
  emitters are original CarbonEngineJS code, with Unity's HLSLcc (MIT) used as a
  behavioral reference.

